{"name":"Little Boy Blue","hex":"#6495da","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"little","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Small, not large, limited, particularly:","Small, limited in size."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Not much.","Not at all."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/little"},{"term":"boy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Bodo (Central Africa)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male child. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A young man."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boy"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Little Boy Blue","blocks":[{"text":"\"Little Boy Blue\" is an English-language nursery rhyme. It has a Roud Folk Song Index number of 11318."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Denslow-little-boy-blue2.jpg/330px-Denslow-little-boy-blue2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Boy_Blue","wikidata":"Q6649245"},{"title":"Little Boy Blue (1912 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Little Boy Blue is a 1912 silent one-reel film produced by Lubin Manufacturing Company and distributed by the General Film Company. The movie was released on May 6, 1912. The movie featured child actor Raymond Hackett assuming the role of Harold and Marie Wierman playing Elizabeth, Harold's older sister."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/LittleBoyBluePic01.jpg/330px-LittleBoyBluePic01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Boy_Blue_(1912_film)","wikidata":"Q124797710"},{"title":"Little Boy","blocks":[{"text":"Little Boy was a type of atomic bomb created by the Manhattan Project during World War II. The name is also often used to describe the specific bomb (L-11) used in the bombing of the Japanese city of Hiroshima by the Boeing B-29 Superfortress Enola Gay on 6 August 1945, making it the first nuclear weapon used in warfare, and the second nuclear explosion in history, after the Trinity nuclear test. It exploded with an energy of approximately 15 kilotons of TNT (63 TJ) and had an explosion radius of approximately 0.81 miles (1.3 km) which caused widespread death and destruction across the city. It was a gun-type fission weapon which used uranium that had been enriched in the fissile isotope uranium-235 to power its explosive reaction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Little_Boy_bomb.jpg/330px-Little_Boy_bomb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Boy","wikidata":"Q181013"},{"title":"Boy","blocks":[{"text":"A boy is a young male human. The term is commonly used for a child or an adolescent. When a male human reaches adulthood, they are usually described as a man."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg/330px-Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy","wikidata":"Q3010"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/TheaterAdLittleBoyBlue1912.jpg/500px-TheaterAdLittleBoyBlue1912.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/TheaterAdLittleBoyBlue1912.jpg/500px-TheaterAd